Step 12 — Send a message to SQS
PURPOSE:
Why?
SQS acts as a buffer/queue between producers and consumers.
Producer
   ↓
SQS
   ↓
Consumer

The producer doesn't have to wait for the consumer to process the message.
Interview answer
"I've used SQS to decouple components and enable asynchronous processing. 
The producer sends messages to the queue, and a consumer such as Lambda processes them independently. 
This also helps with retries and handling temporary downstream failures."
